      "lineNbr": 477,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T22:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- Issue: In the Renode.__init__ method, self._temp_dir \u003d tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() creates an object whose lifecycle is bound to self. If self or self._temp_dir goes out of scope or is garbage collected while renode-ec-launch is running in an asynchronous subprocess, the temporary directory (and renode-uart PTY symlink/socket inside it) will be deleted immediately, causing test failures.\n\n- Impact: Intermittent or silent test failures due to missing UART PTY path during execution.\n\n- Remediation: Explicitly clean up self._temp_dir in Renode.cleanup() rather than relying solely on object garbage collection:\n\n```\ndef cleanup(self) -\u003e None:\n    if self.process:\n        self.process.kill()\n        self.process.wait()\n        self.process \u003d None\n    if os.path.lexists(self.console_pty):\n        try:\n            os.unlink(self.console_pty)\n        except OSError:\n            pass\n    if hasattr(self, \"_temp_dir\") and self._temp_dir:\n        self._temp_dir.cleanup()\n        ```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 468,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 477,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "f8c36f4983c82c1e00e9938ebb67170d5e09d531",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6b24113_949a46ae",
        "filename": "test/run_device_tests.py",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 477,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T22:12:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We must avoid calling self._temp_dir.cleanup() inside Renode.cleanup(). Renode.cleanup() is called after each individual test in flash_and_run_test(), whereas the Renode platform instance (self) is created once in main() and reused across all tests on that board. In Patch Set 10, calling self._temp_dir.cleanup() inside cleanup() deleted the temporary directory after test #1 finished, causing test #2 to fail with FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \u0027/tmp/tmpXXXXXX/renode-uart\u0027 (which caused the CQ failure). Because self is referenced by main() throughout the run, self._temp_dir stays alive while tests execute, and tempfile.TemporaryDirectory automatically cleans up on process exit.",
      "parentUuid": "66d9b67d_9d7d03d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 468,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 477,
        "endChar": 20
